<blockquote>
<p><strong>Knowledge is power, and sharing that knowledge is caring!</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Continuing my bad habit of coldposting every once in a while. I hope you enjoy.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Random&nbsp;author&nbsp;comments</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Access&nbsp;granted!&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;for&nbsp;reading!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>By total coincidence, I went to search the surname &quot;Yin&quot; to be sure it was suitable for this skip and found that its meaning includes &quot;<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Y%C4%ABn_(surname)">flourishing, blood red</a>.&quot;</p>
<p>Also realized I keep using &quot;Site 54&quot; because it wasn't in use and I didn't want to step on anyone's toes, so taking the 5044 slot felt appropriate. <strong>Edit:</strong> I don't know how I came to think this when Site 54 is one of the few numbers listed on the list of sites. Oops. Changing it in the skip.</p>
<p>This is definitely grounded in of one of those thoughts that you have while trying to fall asleep at night. It's an effort to combine a few things that scare me &#8212; particularly, something that is both terrible and easily avoidable. As a kid, I was seriously creeped out by the warning sticker on the side of large buckets showing a toddler drowning in just a few inches of water. The thought of dying because of such a small margin was always chilling. I hope some of that sensation comes across here (even though, as I write this, it's now painfully clear that the toddler-killing bucket is scarier than anything I can dream up).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks to djkaktus for authoring <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-3693">SCP-3693</a> and giving me a better sense of how to describe seeing with your eyes closed.</p>
