<p>Agreeing the tone could use some work. I think the idea of the Foundation finding an anomaly with some practical purpose and trying to put it to use would work, but the paint-by-numbers approach here isn't doing it for me. In particular, the test logs escalation of &quot;it gets spooky and then someone dies&quot; is a major letdown from what is a unique and interesting object effect. -1, I think that if you were to rework the testing logs to take a different direction, like perhaps other things besides non-airtight rooms being affected, that might escalate things in a way that would be more fun to read about.</p>

