			<div class="content" id="post-content-4615663">
									

<p>I like the testing logs. Before I read them I was beginning to think this SCP was to helpful with no downsides. The testing logs were a good demonstration of why a debriefing was required for the use of this scp to be ethical.<br />
The logs could be improved if the D-class were moved to different rooms during the tests. Each room could have an air leak coming from a different location. What did the foundation learn by keeping d-class in the same room with the leak coming from under the door? Right now the logs suggest the Foundation was being cruel for no reason. If the D-class were moved into different nearly air tight rooms, it would show the foundation was using the tests to fix it's airtight rooms. They just didn't think it was necessary to tell the D-class that the blood was representative of air flow. Then they would learn that keeping the d-class in the dark (pun intended) was harmful and change the containment procedures.</p>

							</div>

								
					
